<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Tech stocks plunge as US midterm results fuel fears of tighter AI rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e63f6d3e73398879e0c4df47c622bd874f76bd04b04d940d3af2c18abd8078a4</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T05:02:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20261106-tech-stocks-plunge-us-midterm-ai-rules--18679eaee3e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261106-tech-stocks-plunge-us-midterm-ai-rules" /><summary type="html">Asian tech stocks fell sharply on Friday, with Seoul and Tokyo leading losses after a Wall Street sell-off driven by fears of tighter AI regulation following Democrats’ US midterm election victory. Many winning candidates pledged to curb data centre development amid opposition to the projects from across the political spectrum.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>'Leaders all over the world understand that Trump is only there for two more years &amp; then he's gone'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69e5578ab4f1bf17c99c681c76368c251c3f9f1fdf5d3e8ff7e6f48ea99d6efd</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T04:31:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/leaders-all-over-the-world-understand-that-trump-is-only-there-for-two-more-years-then-he-s-gone--3108ff0afd4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-all-over-the-world-understand-that-trump-is-only-there-for-two-more-years-then-he-s-gone" /><summary type="html">In American politics, even presidential power has its limits. And now, the laws of political gravity may be catching up with Donald Trump's hyper-aggressive exercise of executive authority.
 
Following what political scientist Ian Bremmer describes as the most consequential electoral reversal for a governing party in more than half a century, the founder and CEO of Eurasia Group and GZERO Media argues that the United States has entered a new political phase: the beginning of the end of Trump's ability to dominate the political agenda, at home and abroad.
 
Joining François Picard for a wide-ranging Spotlight interview, Bremmer revisits his provocative thesis that America has already reached "peak Trump." This is not to suggest that the president has become powerless. Rather, Bremmer argues that his political authority is increasingly constrained by an emboldened congressional opposition, growing Republican discontent, unpopular economic and foreign policy decisions, and a dawning realization among world leaders that the clock is ticking on the Trump presidency.
 
The reversal, in Bremmer's account, is extraordinary:
 
"Trump back in 2024 engineered for himself the biggest political comeback in American political history. And now, only two years later, the biggest loss in 50 years."
 
At the heart of his argument lies a fundamental distinction between the formal powers of the presidency and the political influence required to wield them effectively. Trump remains commander-in-chief, commands the machinery of executive government and continues to dominate the media landscape. Yet Bremmer contends that the president's capacity to turn those advantages into lasting political victories and meaningful policy outcomes is rapidly diminishing.
 
The consequences extend far beyond Washington. From the war in Iran and the unresolved conflict in Ukraine to transatlantic relations under extraordinary strain, America's allies and adversaries alike are beginning to recalibrate their strategic calculations, looking beyond the present administration toward the political landscape that will follow.
 
As Bremmer puts it:
 
"Those foreign leaders will start to engage more with the America that they expect to deal with after Trump is gone."
 
At home, Bremmer points to mounting economic disillusionment, the perceived betrayal of campaign promises, and allegations of corruption and self-dealing reminiscent of America's Gilded Age. Together, these forces threaten to erode the electoral coalition that returned Trump to the White House. Meanwhile, the president's apparent preoccupation with monuments, personal projects and his own legacy raises a deeper question: At what point does the spectacle of power begin to undermine the substance of governance?
 
Bremmer also questions the president's capacity to sustain the relentless demands of the office, describing Trump as increasingly distracted and less focused on the issues that matter most. His assessment is stark:
 
"He's focusing on things that don't really matter. And ultimately that's going to weaken his power and weaken his disruptive capacity. Yes, two more years to go. But nowhere near the level of disruption that he had on the global stage at the beginning of this term."
 
The larger question is one of profound significance for American democracy and the international order: Can a president retain the formidable constitutional powers of the world's most consequential political office while progressively losing the political influence needed to exercise them?
 
Donald Trump has built his political identity on superlatives, from the extraordinary comeback that returned him to the White House to his ambitions to reshape the global order. But if Bremmer's diagnosis is correct, the president who once appeared capable of bending political reality to his will may now be confronting a reality he cannot bend: the limits of his own power.
 
The presidency still has two years to run. The era of peak Trump, Bremmer argues, may already be over.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rubio denies plans to resign, says working for Trump until end of term has 'always been my plan'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10f5c1492a61c3327062121f35bf6c043699775142da847fddc6571cec271783</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T00:24:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-marco-rubio-denies-resignation-2028-white-house--dd09aa774082.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-marco-rubio-denies-resignation-2028-white-house" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio dismissed reports on Thursday that he planned to leave the administration after Republican midterm losses, telling The New York Times he intended to serve through the end of President Donald Trump’s term. Rubio, a potential 2028 presidential candidate, declined to discuss his plans.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Three-quarters of world's displaced people face severe climate risks, UN says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab2b8d14c535cd6744d9d7f81b657918f4a85e8e56711b899b820e5e1934ee9f</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T23:34:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261105-un-displaced-people-climate-risks--783288ff5f56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261105-un-displaced-people-climate-risks" /><summary type="html">Nearly 90 million forcibly displaced people, or three-quarters of the global total, live in countries highly exposed to climate hazards, the UN Refugee Agency said on Friday, urging action ahead of the COP31 climate summit in Turkey. It said droughts, floods and extreme heat were making lasting solutions harder to find.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria court bars opposition candidate two months before election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7526378ddfd31f50a1827aa4d08d74df4878fec70bee13ddc1a7ea2344314bfd</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T21:22:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nigeria-court-bars-opposition-candidate-two-months-before-election--30781d646246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-court-bars-opposition-candidate-two-months-before-election" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, a Nigerian court disqualifies a leading presidential candidate, adding fresh complications for the electoral process two months before the election. Also, tens of thousands have fled across the border into Kenya as deadly ethnic clashes in southern Ethiopia intensify. And having fled conflict and violence, members of the first Refugee Youth Olympic Team are chasing Olympic dreams at Dakar 2026.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>French protests: 'It's only when public, private sector act together that you can make changes'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:467ecb66f108c671dcd871754b8eca2f826dae62f476aaddbe282ee8c2b5c66e</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T20:39:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-french-protests-it-s-only-when-public-private-sector-act-together-that-you-can-make-changes--6e39ed1d6297.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-french-protests-it-s-only-when-public-private-sector-act-together-that-you-can-make-changes" /><summary type="html">“You can be as repressive as you want. The grievances are still here.” With this stark observation, Ariane Bogain, lecturer in French and politics at Northumbria University, captures the central dilemma confronting the French government: how can political authority be restored when the social and economic grievances driving public anger remain unresolved? Bogain and French politics editor Marc Perelman join Delano D'Souza to examine a protest movement that has evolved beyond its initial demands over purchasing power, fuel prices and education into a broader challenge to the French government. Perelman identifies a striking political paradox: Marine Le Pen and Jean-Luc Mélenchon, despite occupying opposing ideological positions, are “objective allies” in their shared electoral interest in weakening the political centre.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Inhumane punishment': Governor Gavin Newsom to commute all 548 California death sentences</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a95851c36b292fe5a8d3b0cab46b650396ed6e32f1f7cd3c57f026609bda00d2</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T19:59:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-inhumane-punishment-california-governor-gavin-newsom-to-commute-548-death-sentences--058895c955cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-inhumane-punishment-california-governor-gavin-newsom-to-commute-548-death-sentences" /><summary type="html">California Governor Gavin Newsom on Thursday said he would commute all 548 death sentences in the state to life in prison without parole, marking a major step away from capital punishment as he prepares to leave office after eight years.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal: Cristiano Ronaldo announces his international retirement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a1a7d3f389da930269ef440558eb084a4a0da2f992848aa2b13d9a98c0d426</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T18:16:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-portugal-cristiano-ronaldo-announces-his-international-retirement--859e2abfc037.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-portugal-cristiano-ronaldo-announces-his-international-retirement" /><summary type="html">Portuguese football legend Cristiano Ronaldo announced on Thursday he was retiring from international football at the age of 41.</summary></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Civilians under fire from military junta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14de4b445645909489629a901c2a9cbf662eac174739b03cf736a3e4156b7705</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:58:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-myanmar-civilians-under-fire-from-military-junta--4174803e3ee2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-myanmar-civilians-under-fire-from-military-junta" /><summary type="html">More than five years after the military coup, the junta launched a new offensive in September to retake Rakhine State, intensifying airstrikes against civilians and employing double-tap strikes</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>France needs 'more public services', 'salaries are too low', 'schools are in very, very bad shape'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2315d1cc7a8cd95664c6b019c0754b9da02f500a407964f553f14773c8bd323e</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:36:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-needs-more-public-services-salaries-are-too-low-schools-are-in-very-very-bad-shape--af87d6700bce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-needs-more-public-services-salaries-are-too-low-schools-are-in-very-very-bad-shape" /><summary type="html">As France confronts another wave of strikes and protests, Gaëlle Martinez, National Secretary of the trade union Solidaires, presents the general strike as more than a confrontation over wages, public spending or the cost of living. Her account reveals a deeper struggle over economic dignity, the future of public services and the democratic right to collective protest. “People just want to live, not survive.” For Martinez, deteriorating schools, insufficient salaries and the dismantling of public services are not isolated policy failures. They are interconnected symptoms of political and economic priorities that, in her assessment, place fiscal restraint above social welfare. Her demand for “a new budget” that is “not based on cuts” is accompanied by a call to “tax the biggest companies, the richest companies where the profits are made.”</summary></entry><entry><title>Paraguay's president Pena impeached after resigning over banking scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3127f96a66305f8a2ce307f933206f4df57c3acd303b87c485c4d40fac470952</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:33:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-paraguay-s-president-pe_a-impeached-moments-after-resigning-amid-banking-scandal--498613eca0a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-paraguay-s-president-pe%C3%B1a-impeached-moments-after-resigning-amid-banking-scandal" /><summary type="html">Paraguay’s lower house voted unanimously to impeach President Santiago Pena on Thursday, just minutes after he announced his resignation on X. Protesters have rallied in the streets since the takeover of a bank linked to Pena blocked millions of people, including pensioners, from accessing their money.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Interior ministry says 600,000 protest across France as unions claim 'close to 1.6 million'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cf31ca3a2debc2182917744d54a0dc73268c1ddda9faa8a72eee5102f2e406b</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:05:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261105-live-france-nationwide-strikes-living-costs--b8adf3b2e07a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261105-live-france-nationwide-strikes-living-costs" /></entry><entry><title>Navi Pillay: Fighting violence with justice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91ebe7153a4b066523d4bdd8c3f4c22a1386485f14d4ed75af34b2276f8b628d</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T16:12:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/navi-pillay-fighting-violence-with-justice--5c93068ee314.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/navi-pillay-fighting-violence-with-justice" /><summary type="html">From the International Criminal Court to Africa’s place in the global justice system, the stakes are high. In an exclusive interview, Nobel Peace Prize winner, Navi Pillay will discuss international justice . She says it it must not be held hostage to political power, as Donald Trump targets the ICC. What does this showdown mean for Africa?</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: 'Donald Trump's wings have been more than clipped'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9742b6d24e9cfbc5d2dab6ff133dd7f1c451ebe79b425c0f9f794660e30a647c</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:46:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-donald-trump-s-wings-have-been-more-than-clipped--c82ffc4a0687.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-donald-trump-s-wings-have-been-more-than-clipped" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump faced a radically transformed and hostile political landscape after Democrats seized both the House of Representatives and the Senate in Tuesday's (November 3) midterms. The result was a personal humiliation for the 80-year-old Trump, leaving him as a lame duck president for the remaining two years of his term. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Global travel sector grows despite headwinds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284dcfa6cf4a463099ca3e99cc909e9c32f0338cf0774615da9bb706a9c28807</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:43:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261105-global-travel-sector-grows-despite-headwinds--09523e257418.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261105-global-travel-sector-grows-despite-headwinds" /><summary type="html">The global tourism sector is growing, despite conflicts and economic uncertainty. That's the finding of a new report by World Travel Market, which says the number of international arrivals is set to hit a record 1.57 billion in 2026.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>Europe: Dozens of flights diverted following bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a10375269a1c9724055da1d000603a831071253d5f945753679fc74d5ea97810</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:40:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-europe-dozens-of-flights-diverted-following-bomb-threats--ede05126082f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-europe-dozens-of-flights-diverted-following-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Hoax bomb threats hit at least 27 affected flights around Europe this week.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Identity crisis': Can Democrats 'deliver' following their 'historic', once in a generation victory?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e4cae9ba8769a7cef2b5fd922ada74c3d8f1cce582d8876f94d3ed3ef11d3c</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:27:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/identity-crisis-can-democrats-deliver-following-their-historic-once-in-a-generation-victory--c1d1ab999d50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/identity-crisis-can-democrats-deliver-following-their-historic-once-in-a-generation-victory" /><summary type="html">A historic Democratic electoral breakthrough has transformed the American political landscape. For Laurie Dundon, Senior Associate Fellow at the European Leadership Network and former US diplomat, the central question is whether the Democratic Party can convert electoral momentum into coherent governance. "Can they deliver?" Dunden examines the apparent disintegration of Donald Trump's 2024 MAGA coalition alongside the Democratic Party's continuing ideological struggle between its progressive and centrist wings. Ahead of 2028, Dunden cautions against seeing Trump as a lame duck: "Trump is never going to stop being Trump." The resulting struggle over congressional spending powers, presidential vetoes, tariffs and investigations promises to be a delicate dance to watch".</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's Arab list backs Eisenkot as Netanyahu loses ultra-Orthodox support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b3a217a92516f48ab7d5429111f499ccd4336d6d4332247d9eb62c8bcaab863</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:43:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election--3aadbd4431d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election" /><summary type="html">Israel's largest Arab party grouping said Thursday it would recommend opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot to form the next government, potentially bolstering his bid after Arab-majority lists won a record 19 seats in last week's election and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lost the support of an allied religious party.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Bringing the magic of Harry Potter to life through music</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5be4b83cfef1df705001e57b56f1ef3f87ed56687787d33e0bc53aac3175350</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:30:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261105-bringing-the-magic-of-harry-potter-to-life-through-music--52c3b9b96588.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261105-bringing-the-magic-of-harry-potter-to-life-through-music" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Entre Nous, we meet Timothy Henty, the British conductor bringing the magic of Harry Potter to life in Paris. As part of the Harry Potter Film Concert Series, he leads more than 80 musicians in a spectacular live orchestral performance, offering audiences a unique opportunity to experience one of cinema's most beloved stories like never before.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>British comedian Russell Brand found guilty of rape, sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6950bfff5e5a4e2259acebb494fcd80dea7974984e8c69a30a0325149a8aa02b</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:26:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261105-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-sexual-assault--557036caf804.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261105-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-sexual-assault" /><summary type="html">A London jury on Thursday convicted British comedian and actor Russell Brand of one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France faces new protests as government seeks to prevent violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8df3ddb1483fe36198d8390011b7c7b735012f18ef9b01bbebddc56bbfb213f</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:19:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-faces-new-protests-as-government-seeks-to-prevent-violence--726573d2b4a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-faces-new-protests-as-government-seeks-to-prevent-violence" /><summary type="html">France faces new protests as the government seeks to prevent a repeat of October unrest. Protesters demand better public services, including education, and also critique the rising cost-of-living. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>French bank hit by cyberattack, hackers steal $100 million</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae1e6231c78bd7e9b4b2f67242fede5918f731202088eedc363ad3794be8eda3</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:09:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/cyberattack-french-bank-says-online-hacking-stole-around-100-million--5c60fc9f98d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cyberattack-french-bank-says-online-hacking-stole-around-100-million" /><summary type="html">French regional bank Crédit Mutuel Arkéa said Wednesday it had been hit by a cyberattack that led to fraudulent transfers worth around 100 million euros ($112 million). The bank said the attack, which has since been "contained", allowed hackers to access its own accounts and transfer funds to other banks. Customer accounts were not affected, and no losses were reported by clients.</summary></entry><entry><title>South African star Zolani Mahola: From 'Waka Waka' with Shakira to 'People Power'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa1b9ed95c33ba0c2cdca2096f7a24ffd5d668af202367588af6b75a40c9122c</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T13:34:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261105-south-african-star-zolani-mahola-from-waka-waka-with-shakira-to-people-power--ed19464c0334.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261105-south-african-star-zolani-mahola-from-waka-waka-with-shakira-to-people-power" /><summary type="html">From the global success of "Waka Waka" to her forthcoming second solo album "People Power", South Africa's Zolani Mahola has built a career around the power of music to bring people together.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>'It's fascinating to see a human becoming a person': Author Clémentine Goldszal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e25e7a8e0a5f00e0adf0142e83185bd83c1959d7acb47a9b0395b0b2758a54a</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T13:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261105-it-s-fascinating-to-see-a-human-becoming-a-person-author-cl_mentine-goldszal--263c6b475a1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261105-it-s-fascinating-to-see-a-human-becoming-a-person-author-cl%C3%A9mentine-goldszal" /><summary type="html">What is life like for a newly born, premature or sick baby? These are the questions tackled by a French journalist in her first ever book. Clémentine Goldszal asks what it means to be rushed from the delivery room to the neonatal intensive care unit, and what is means to enter the world before you are ready. Goldszal's book is entitled "Newborn: Inside the World of Neonatal Care". She spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry></feed>
